# Frontend Design

- Match the existing design system, spacing, typography, density, controls, and interaction patterns before adding new UI.
- Build the actual usable surface rather than marketing or explanatory screens.
- Use restrained, domain-appropriate visuals; avoid generic decorative gradients, nested cards, and one-note palettes.
- Ensure text fits across mobile and desktop, controls are keyboard-reachable, and states are clear.
- Verify meaningful UI changes with browser or screenshot evidence when a local runtime is available.
